-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC # Creating Genie Spaces
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Databricks Genie Spaces enable business users to interact with data using questions and answers powered by a Large Language Model(LLM). End users can ask questions in natural language and receive answers in text and visualizations.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Prerequisites
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC In this notebook, we will create a Genie space to interact with the TPC-DI dataset. In order to follow along, you must have run through the TPC-DI ingestion process, as outlined in the *02.1 Ingesting Data* notebook.

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Creating a Genie Space
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Access Genie by selecting it from the left sidebar.<br>
-- MAGIC    ![Genie menu item](Includes/images/genie/sidebar.png)
-- MAGIC 1. Create a new space by clicking **New** in the top-right corner.
-- MAGIC 1. Specify the data to which to connect the Genie space:
-- MAGIC    * Select your personal catalog.
-- MAGIC    * Choose the *tpcdi_dbsql_10* schema.
-- MAGIC    * Select the *dimcustomer* table.<p>
-- MAGIC    * Click **Create**.<br>
-- MAGIC    ![Connecct data dialog](Includes/images/genie/configurespace.png)
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Your Genie space is now ready to use!

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## Interacting with your data
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC With a Genie space created, we can now begin asking questions of our data in plain language.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Let's begin with a simple example. Try submitting a prompt like this: *Show me all the customer data.*</br>
-- MAGIC    ![Data tab](Includes/images/genie/firstprompt.png)
-- MAGIC 1. A response is generated. Click the **Show code** button to expose the SQL code that was generated to satisfy the request. This show us that users can ask questions in plain English, and through Databricks’s LLM-powered processing Engine, this gets translated into SQL that will provide answers, or that you can customize further. This capability dramatically lowers the bar for generating quick insights for both data workers and business users. <br>
-- MAGIC    ![Data tab](Includes/images/genie/showcode.png)
-- MAGIC 1. Let's try a different prompt. This time, submit a prompt like this: *Show me the distribution of customers based on gender.*</br>
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC **NOTE:** Databricks continuously improves the underlying large language model that Genie uses to generate responses. Genie may provide data previews and suggested visualizations that vary depending on the dataset. The type and behavior of these visualizations may differ each time, allowing you to adjust them according to your needs.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC    ![Data tab](Includes/images/genie/secondprompt.png)<br>
-- MAGIC    Notice how this time a visualization is generated as part of the response..

-- COMMAND ----------

-- MAGIC %md
-- MAGIC ## History
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Using the history, you can access all the previous conversations in the same Genie space. 
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Click the **History** button in the top-right corner.<br>
-- MAGIC    ![History button](Includes/images/genie/historybutton.png)<br>
-- MAGIC    This will show you a historical list of conversations, so that you can monitor the activity within your space, understand errors, feedback, and results the space is returning for your users.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC 1. Select a conversation to revisit it. From here, you can review the conversation or even continue it. For example, let's submit a new prompt: *Show the distribution of customers by status as a bar chart.*<br>
-- MAGIC    ![Add a visualization](Includes/images/genie/showbarchart.png)
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC As we can see, a conversation can be continued since Genie remembers the context of the conversation that you've reopened.

